  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...\nThursday\u2019s weather maker is currently an impressive hurricane \nforce extratropical cyclone located near 44N 175W. This system \nwill continue to travel east through the next few days but weaken \nas it moves into the Gulf, with the low center west of Dixon \nEntrance by Thursday morning. Overall confidence is high in the \nlocation of this system, with a wide range of pressure depth \nsolutions; currently thinking the low will reach near 985mb by \nThursday morning. As this system lifts north along the Alexander \nArchipelago coast expect outflow winds to start to diminish thru \nthe Inner Channels, with another round of precipitation into \nSaturday morning. Currently not expecting any widespread snow \nimpacts at sea level, warm air should have successfully \ninfiltrated most areas across the Panhandle with the exception of \nHaines and Skagway highways. Look for a break in precipitation \nSunday.\n\nBy the weekend, powerful swell from distant storms will continue \nto impact our coast; however, winds and fresh seas should be \ntrending down. Look for our next large low to move into the Gulf \nby Monday or Tuesday of next week.",
